        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions (Technical)</h2>

        <p><strong>How much pressure is inside an aerosol can?</strong><br>
            Typically 3&ndash;8 bar at 20&deg;C depending on propellant type and product category.
        </p>

        <p><strong>Can aerosol cans explode?</strong><br>
            Yes, if exposed to temperatures beyond design limits or if manufacturing defects exist. Properly
            manufactured cans include significant safety margins.
        </p>

        <p><strong>Why do some aerosols spray as foam?</strong><br>
            Foaming depends on surfactant formulation combined with actuator air-mixing design.
        </p>

        <p><strong>What is the safest aerosol propellant?</strong><br>
            Compressed gases and BOV systems offer the highest safety but may compromise spray consistency and cost.
        </p>

        <p><strong>Is aerosol manufacturing profitable in India?</strong><br>
            Yes, when technical design, safety compliance, and formulation performance are correctly balanced.
        </p>

